Setup Notes: Offline / Unreachable PE Server Preparation
Goal: Install the Puppet agent package, pre-populate /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf with your intended target server and certname, and enable the service—without running puppet agent -t against the server yet.

Why puppet agent -t is skipped now: A full run requires resolving and reaching TCP port 8140 on the PE primary server and signing the CSR before fetching a catalog.

1
Add the Puppet Repository and Install puppet-agent
Run these commands on your Azure VM to add the Puppet release repository for your Ubuntu release and install puppet-agent:

Bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y curl ca-certificates lsb-release
curl -fsSL "https://apt.puppet.com/puppet8-release-$(lsb_release -cs).deb" -o /tmp/puppet-release.deb
sudo dpkg -i /tmp/puppet-release.deb
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y puppet-agent
Verification: /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet --version prints the installed version number.

2
Write Pre-Configured puppet.conf
Populate /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf with placeholder or planned values for server, certname, and environment so you only need to adjust values if plans change:

Bash
sudo tee /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf >/dev/null <<'EOF'
[main]
server = <onprem-pe-server-fqdn>
certname = <agent-certname>
environment = production
EOF
Verification: sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet config print server certname environment outputs the values you wrote into puppet.conf.

3
Enable the puppet Service Without Triggering a Server Run
Enable the puppet service so it is set to start at boot, while leaving puppet agent -t until network access to the on-prem PE server is ready:

Bash
sudo /opt/puppetlabs/puppet/bin/puppet resource service puppet enable=true
Verification: systemctl is-enabled puppet outputs enabled (or systemctl status puppet shows it inactive/waiting without attempting a remote catalog fetch).

Quick Reference Cheatsheet (For Later When Server Is Reachable)
Config file path: /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf

Check effective config: sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet config print all

Send CSR / run agent: sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet agent -t (run on the agent after connectivity and CSR signing are in place)

For extra reference on puppet.conf and agent installation on Ubuntu, you can search YouTube for "puppet.conf configuration example Ubuntu" or "install puppet-agent Ubuntu".
